        },
        "pageimage": "Looking_Backward.jpg",
        "extract": "Looking Backward: 2000–1887 is a utopian time travel science fiction novel by the American journalist and writer Edward Bellamy first published in 1888.\nThe book was translated into several languages, and in short order \"sold a million copies.\" According to historian Daniel Immerwahr, \"In the 19th-century United States, only Uncle Tom's Cabin sold more copies in its first years\" than Bellamy's book. \nThe novel inspired several utopian communities. In the United States alone, over 162 \"Bellamy Clubs\" sprang up to discuss and propagate the book's ideas. According to Erich Fromm, \"It is one of the few books ever published that created almost immediately...",
